  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "round-heads-sahara-s004-p00072",
      "source_en": "In Libya the dates of the earliest pottery are even more recent, at Uan Tabu in the Acacus they were 14C dated at 8,950+55 BP and in Uan Afuda at 8,790+93 BP (Roset 1983, 1996; Mori 2000; Le Quellec 2006b). The earliest Saharan pottery is associated with settlements with no evidence of domestic food production but the economy was based instead on hunting and gathering.",
